 ## Overview
-The TVAM Integrator is a base class for volumetric integrators in Tomographic Volumetric Additive Manufacturing (TVAM) that manages projector ray sampling, time sampling, and switching between regular and stochastic sampling modes [S1, unofficial]. It serves as the foundation for specialized integrators like the [CornerIntegrator](7445-cornerintegrator.md) and [Radon Integrator](7470-radon-integrator.md) by providing the infrastructure for sampling rays from projector emitters and handling the temporal sequence of light patterns [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard volume rendering integrators, it explicitly accounts for the discrete nature of Digital Micromirror Device (DMD) pixels and the temporal multiplexing of projection patterns [S1, unofficial].
+The TVAM Integrator is a base class for volumetric integrators designed for Tomographic Volumetric Additive Manufacturing (TVAM) [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of simulating light transport from projector emitters through a photosensitive resin volume to calculate polymerization doses [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard camera-based ray casting, it samples rays from projector emitters and incorporates manufacturing physics, such as polymerization thresholds and inhibitor dynamics, into the integrand [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from siblings like the Radon Integrator by providing the foundational sampling infrastructure and physical model evaluation, while specialized variants like the CornerIntegrator handle specific boundary conditions [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-The integrator prepares rays for emission from projector emitters, samples their positions and times, and computes initial weights based on the sampling strategy. It relies on a scene containing a target shape and a single interior medium [S1, unofficial].
+The integrator manages the lifecycle of ray generation for projector-based volume rendering, handling both regular and stochastic sampling modes, and evaluates a physical model for polymerization based on accumulated light dose.
 
